# root-and-branch Phase 4 (2026-08-15, K3b): REGENERATED test artifacts. These five files are rewritten by
# every run of test-edfiRoundTrip.js / test-sifRoundTrip.js (the last run's twin observations and verdicts).
# They are evidence of the last run, not fixtures — nothing reads them back — so they are untracked: a
# regenerated artifact must never double as a fixture (Phase 1 lesson) and must never ride into a commit
# (Phase 3 W3/W4). The suites keep writing them in place; the cited paths in the DEVLOGs stay valid.
educoreForge/forges/edfi/test/test-artifacts/roundTripGateTwinObservations.log
educoreForge/forges/sif/test/test-artifacts/sifRoundTripFixtureClean.verdict.json
educoreForge/forges/sif/test/test-artifacts/sifRoundTripTwin-deletedField.report.json
educoreForge/forges/sif/test/test-artifacts/sifRoundTripTwin-injectedField.report.json
educoreForge/forges/sif/test/test-artifacts/sifRoundTripTwin-orderSwap.report.json
# Phase 4 review V1 (2026-08-15): four MORE files rewritten by every suite run, found by mtime after the fleet
# (their bytes happened to match, so the tree looked clean): sifRoundTrip's twin log + probes; cedsHubForge's
# two reports (written, parsed back in the same run, never a cross-run fixture). Same rule, same treatment.
educoreForge/forges/sif/test/test-artifacts/sifRoundTripGateTwinObservations.log
educoreForge/forges/sif/test/test-artifacts/p4CharacteristicsProbes.json
educoreForge/forges/ceds/test/test-artifacts/cedsHubSkipReport.json
educoreForge/forges/ceds/test/test-artifacts/cedsProseDivergence.json

